---
/**
 * Explains inquiry data handling.
 *
 * Dependencies: BaseLayout.
 * Depended on by: Form consent context and the footer.
 * Why this exists: Visitors need plain-language privacy expectations before submitting details.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy | Justin LeBlanc" canonicalPath="/privacy/">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Only share what the event needs.</h1>
      <p>
        Share only the details that help us talk about your event.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <article class="section reading-shell prose">
    <h2>Information the inquiry uses</h2>
    <p>
      The form asks for contact information, event details, performance time, sound or equipment
      needs, optional budget and special requests, and consent to follow up. Billing details are not
      required to capture an inquiry. Do not submit payment-card data or sensitive personal records.
    </p>

    <h2>Why it is used</h2>
    <p>
      Submitted details are used to review the event and respond to the inquiry. Marketing consent
      is separate, optional, and unchecked.
    </p>

    <h2>Private notifications</h2>
    <p>The inquiry alert is sent only to Justin at his protected business inbox. If Justin separately authorizes Gmail and ChatGPT notifications in his own account, those services may process a privacy-conscious alert; the website does not send customer details directly to ChatGPT.</p>

    <h2>Storage and retention</h2>
    <p>
      The event form keeps an unsent draft in this browser session so a visitor can move between
      steps. The server stores a submitted record only after it returns an inquiry reference.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      Names, email addresses, phone numbers, event dates, venue notes, free text, and invoice
      contents must not be sent in analytics payloads.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions and final policy</h2>
    <p>
      Use Justin's <a href="https://justinleblancmusic.com/contact" rel="external">contact page</a>{" "}
      for questions about an existing inquiry.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
